30,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"Oh boy, the ground is tricky! The firms are worried about clay and slippage for big jobs, but small work is fine. Also, we can't hoard the center or main gate easily.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"My findings are quite telling. People mostly stick to firm ground to reach the tram, and the drainage is struggling, especially with the heat in August.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Minato,,"I found out we have very few groundskeepers left, but we have some nice volunteer groups who like doing habitat work and sports refereeing.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Minako,,"It's a mixed bag. The old overflow basin is still great, but the paved areas are cracking and the eastern avenue trees mostly died from lack of watering.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The financial picture is sobering. Planted areas cost triple to maintain compared to hard surfaces, and the habitat fund only pays for planting and water, not buildings.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, if people only use the firm ground, maybe we shouldn't do too much fancy landscaping in the middle?","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, precisely. And given the drainage issues and heat, a plan that ignores water management would be a folly.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Jonathan, does the habitat fund mean we can't have a big visitor center or something?","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Minato, Jonathan's data suggests that. Also, my findings show that if we plant too many trees without a plan, they'll just die like the ones on the avenue.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Minato"",""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minato, yes, the fund is very specific. We must be careful not to create a beautiful space that the city cannot afford to maintain or water.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Minako, you said the overflow basin is still good. Maybe we should do more of that?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, that would align with the drainage problems I found. A water-focused approach seems logically sound.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Minato,,"@Benjamin, the volunteers I found love habitat work! They might be able to help with a project like that.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Minato, that is a helpful point. If the staff is low, volunteers are essential for survival.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, I agree. But we must remember that water-managed ground is the most expensive to maintain per hectare.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
