55,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"Looking at the plans, the Wetland Restoration seems cool, but the Market Plaza is easier to build since it's mostly flat. But the Sports Terraces might be too big for the clay!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,The Market Plaza ignores the heat and drainage issues. The Woodland Walk risks the same death toll as the eastern avenue. Wetland Restoration addresses the water and the tram-crossers.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Minato,,I like the Wetland Restoration because the habitat volunteers can help! The Sports Terraces are also good because of the youth league volunteers.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Minako,,The Market Plaza is just more paving that will crack like the civic hall apron. The Woodland Walk is a watering nightmare. Wetland Restoration is the most durable.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The Wetland Restoration is funded by the habitat fund, which is great for the initial cost. However, the upkeep is high. The Market Plaza is cheaper to maintain.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Jonathan, but if the Market Plaza is just paving, will it be too hot? Benjamin said August was really hot.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Jonathan"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, exactly. A paved plaza would be a heat island. The Wetland Restoration uses the natural drainage and provides cooling.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Jonathan, if the habitat fund pays for the start, maybe the volunteers can help keep the costs down later?","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Minato, that's a fair hope. Given the failure of the trees and the success of the basin, the Wetland plan is the only one with a proven track record.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, I see your point. While the upkeep is higher, the initial funding makes it viable, and it avoids the cost of replacing dead trees.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"I'm leaning toward the Wetland Restoration. It's small-plant work, so the firms won't struggle with the clay as much as the Sports Terraces.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,It is the only plan that respects the movement of the people and the reality of the climate. I am convinced.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Minato,,I'll go with the Wetland Restoration too! It sounds peaceful and the volunteers will be happy.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Minako,,It is the most logical choice for longevity. I vote for the Wetland Restoration.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,I can accept the higher upkeep if the capital is covered by the fund. I also vote for the Wetland Restoration.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,4,talk,Kenji,,I'm ready to vote!,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I am as well.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,4,talk,Minato,,Me too!,"{""words"":2,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,4,talk,Minako,,Agreed.,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,Let us proceed.,"{""words"":3,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
